Spec: Persistence Module

Purpose:
  Save and restore project state across sessions using IndexedDB auto-save
  and manual .laser project file export/import.

Structure:
  ./auto-save.ts: IndexedDB auto-save, session restore, project file I/O
  ./project-format.ts: Serialization, deserialization, validation

Owns:
  ./auto-save.ts
  ./project-format.ts

Must:
  Auto-save triggers 500ms after any history change.
  Validate project files on import (version, shape count, file size).
  Deserialize shapes back to proper class instances (PathShape, TextObject, GroupShape).
  Notify user on save/restore failures via Toast.
  Support .laser JSON format with version, shapes, layers, material, metadata.

Must not:
  Silently discard corrupted data without notifying the user.
  Allow importing projects that exceed MAX_SHAPES (10000) or MAX_FILE_SIZE (50MB).
  Store sensitive data in IndexedDB or project files.

Depends on:
  IndexedDB (browser API)
  @useStore
  @PathShape.fromJSON
  @TextObject.fromJSON
  @GroupShape.fromJSON
  @notify (Toast)

Scenario: auto-save triggers after shape creation
  Given the canvas has 3 shapes
  When a new rectangle is created
  Then IndexedDB is updated within 500ms
  And the saved project contains 4 shapes

Scenario: session restore on reload
  Given the canvas has 2 shapes and auto-save has run
  When the user reloads the page
  Then the 2 shapes are restored from IndexedDB
  And the canvas renders them correctly

Scenario: export .laser project file
  Given the canvas has shapes, layers, and material dimensions
  When the user exports a .laser project file
  Then a JSON file is downloaded
  And it contains version, shapes array, layers, and material

Scenario: import valid .laser project file
  Given a valid .laser file with 5 shapes
  When the user imports the file
  Then the canvas is populated with 5 shapes
  And layers and material settings are restored

Scenario: corrupted project rejected on import
  Given a .laser file with version field missing
  When the user imports the file
  Then a validation error notification is shown
  And the canvas state is unchanged

Scenario: oversized project rejected
  Given a .laser file exceeding MAX_FILE_SIZE (50MB)
  When the user imports the file
  Then a validation error is shown
  And the canvas state is unchanged

Scenario: shape deserialization preserves types
  Given a project with PathShape, TextObject, and GroupShape
  When the project is saved and reloaded
  Then each shape retains its correct class (PathShape, TextObject, GroupShape)
  And methods like getBounds() work on restored shapes
